            <ArticleTitle>Successful revascularization of a long chronic total occlusion with blunt microdissection complicated by coronary artery dissection.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>673-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of successful percutaneous revascularization of a chronic total occlusion using the LuMend Frontrunner catheter. The case was complicated by a long coronary artery dissection, with inability to access the true lumen. With favorable healing at 7 weeks, the true lumen was accessible which led to procedural success.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
